{
  "title": "PowerSync: Self-Hosted Overview",
  "uid": "powersync-self-hosted-overview",
  "tags": [
    "powersync",
    "observability"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "timezone": "",
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "builtIn": 1,
        "type": "dashboard",
        "enable": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "DS_PROM",
        "label": "AMP (Prometheus)",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "DS_CW",
        "label": "CloudWatch",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "cloudwatch",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "cluster",
        "label": "PowerSync cluster",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(powersync_concurrent_connections, cluster)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {}
      },
      {
        "name": "level",
        "label": "Log level",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "debug,info,warn,error,fatal",
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "ecs_cluster",
        "label": "ECS cluster name",
        "type": "constant",
        "query": "powersync-cluster",
        "current": {
          "text": "powersync-cluster",
          "value": "powersync-cluster"
        },
        "hide": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "api_service",
        "label": "API ECS service",
        "type": "constant",
        "query": "powersync-api",
        "current": {
          "text": "powersync-api",
          "value": "powersync-api"
        },
        "hide": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "repl_service",
        "label": "Replication ECS service",
        "type": "constant",
        "query": "powersync-replication",
        "current": {
          "text": "powersync-replication",
          "value": "powersync-replication"
        },
        "hide": 2
      },
      {
        "name": "alb",
        "label": "Load balancer",
        "description": "Auto-discovered ALB LoadBalancer dimension value.",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "cloudwatch",
          "uid": "${DS_CW}"
        },
        "query": "dimension_values(us-east-1,AWS/ApplicationELB,RequestCount,LoadBalancer)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {}
      },
      {
        "name": "targetgroup",
        "label": "Target group",
        "description": "Auto-discovered ALB TargetGroup dimension value (needed for HealthyHostCount).",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "cloudwatch",
          "uid": "${DS_CW}"
        },
        "query": "dimension_values(us-east-1,AWS/ApplicationELB,HealthyHostCount,TargetGroup)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {},
        "hide": 2
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Service health (SLOs)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Replication lag (now)",
      "id": 10,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 30
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 60
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(powersync_replication_lag_seconds{cluster=~\"$cluster\"})"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How far behind the source database PowerSync is right now. A change written to the source reaches clients after about this long.\n\n**Healthy:** Green, under 30 seconds. Short spikes during large writes or bulk imports are normal.\n\n**If not:** Amber is 30 to 60 seconds, red is over 60 seconds. If it stays high or keeps growing, check the Replicator logs and the source database load. See [Replication lag](https://docs.powersync.com/maintenance-ops/replication-lag)."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Replicator up",
      "id": 11,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green"
                },
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(count(powersync_replication_lag_seconds{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}) > bool 0)"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Whether the replicator is running and sending metrics.\n\n**Healthy:** UP.\n\n**If not:** DOWN means nothing new reaches clients. Check that the replication task is running in ECS and read the [Replicator] Recent logs panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "API healthy hosts",
      "id": 12,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${DS_CW}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "region": "default",
          "namespace": "AWS/ApplicationELB",
          "metricName": "HealthyHostCount",
          "statistic": "Minimum",
          "dimensions": {
            "LoadBalancer": "$alb",
            "TargetGroup": "$targetgroup"
          },
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How many API tasks the load balancer can send client traffic to.\n\n**Healthy:** The same number as the running API tasks (see API running task count).\n\n**If not:** 0 means clients cannot connect at all. A number lower than the running tasks means some tasks fail their health check. Read the [API] Recent logs panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Concurrent connections",
      "id": 13,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(powersync_concurrent_connections{cluster=~\"$cluster\"})"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How many clients are connected and syncing right now, over all API tasks. This number also drives API autoscaling.\n\n**Healthy:** Follows your user activity, for example higher during the day.\n\n**If not:** A sudden drop to 0 while users are active means clients cannot connect. Check API healthy hosts and API 5xx rate.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Ops synced / s",
      "id": 14,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(powersync_operations_synced_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m]))"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How many changes (operations) PowerSync sends to clients per second, averaged over 5 minutes. One operation is one row created, updated or deleted on one client.\n\n**Healthy:** Any value. A high number only means a busy app. 'No data' or 0 when no clients are syncing is normal.\n\n**If not:** Compare with Concurrent connections. Many connections but 0 operations for a long time, while the source data changes, can mean sync is stuck."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "API 5xx rate",
      "id": 15,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${DS_CW}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "region": "default",
          "namespace": "AWS/ApplicationELB",
          "metricName": "HTTPCode_Target_5XX_Count",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "LoadBalancer": "$alb"
          },
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Server errors (HTTP 5xx) that the API sent back to clients.\n\n**Healthy:** 0.\n\n**If not:** Any value above 0 means some client requests failed. Read the [API] Recent logs panel and the [API] Error rate by level panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Replication pipeline",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "id": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Replication lag",
      "id": 20,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 30
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 60
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max by (instance_id) (powersync_replication_lag_seconds{cluster=~\"$cluster\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance_id}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Replication lag over time: how far behind the source database PowerSync is.\n\n**Healthy:** Flat and low (seconds). Short spikes during bulk writes that come back down are normal.\n\n**If not:** A line that keeps going up means PowerSync cannot keep up with the source database. See [Replication lag](https://docs.powersync.com/maintenance-ops/replication-lag)."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Replicated / s (rows \u00b7 transactions \u00b7 chunks)",
      "id": 21,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(powersync_rows_replicated_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "rows/s"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(powersync_transactions_replicated_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "transactions/s"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "sum(rate(powersync_chunks_replicated_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "chunks/s"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How much PowerSync reads from the source database per second. **Rows** are changed rows. **Transactions** are committed transactions. **Chunks** are the batches PowerSync receives from the database's replication stream. The database sends about one empty chunk per second even when nothing changes, so chunks stay above 0 when the app is idle.\n\n**Healthy:** Rows and transactions go up and down with your app's write activity.\n\n**If not:** Rows and transactions at 0 while your app writes to the source database means replication is stuck. Check Replication lag and the [Replicator] Recent logs panel. See [Replication lag](https://docs.powersync.com/maintenance-ops/replication-lag)."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Data replicated (bytes/s)",
      "id": 22,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(powersync_data_replicated_bytes_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "replicated"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How many bytes of changed data PowerSync reads from the source database per second.\n\n**Healthy:** Goes up and down with write activity in the source database.\n\n**If not:** Large steady values with growing Replication lag can mean the writes are too big for the replicator. Compare with Replicated / s."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Replicator restarts (Starting Replication Engine)",
      "id": 23,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${DS_CW}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${DS_CW}"
          },
          "queryMode": "Logs",
          "region": "default",
          "logGroupNames": [
            "/ecs/powersync-replication"
          ],
          "expression": "filter @message like /Starting Replication Engine/ | stats count() as restarts by bin(1h)",
          "statsGroups": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How many times the replicator started, per hour. Each deploy, task replacement or crash causes one start.\n\n**Healthy:** A start only when you deploy or change the service.\n\n**If not:** Repeated starts without a deploy mean the replicator crashes and restarts. Read the [Replicator] Recent logs panel for the error before each start."
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Client sync / API",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "id": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Concurrent connections",
      "id": 30,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(powersync_concurrent_connections{cluster=~\"$cluster\"})",
          "legendFormat": "connections"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How many clients are connected and syncing over time, over all API tasks. This number drives API autoscaling.\n\n**Healthy:** Follows your user activity.\n\n**If not:** A sudden drop while users are active means clients cannot connect. A sudden spike can come from all clients reconnecting after a deploy or a network problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sync throughput (ops/s \u00b7 bytes/s)",
      "id": 31,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "data synced/s"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "Bps"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "ops synced/s"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "ops"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.axisPlacement",
                "value": "right"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(powersync_operations_synced_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "ops synced/s"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(powersync_data_synced_bytes_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "data synced/s"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How much PowerSync sends to clients per second. **Ops synced** (right axis) is the number of row changes. **Data synced** (left axis) is their size in bytes, before compression.\n\n**Healthy:** Follows client activity: high when many clients sync or do their first sync, low when idle.\n\n**If not:** A big rise without more users or more data changes can mean clients download everything again, for example after a sync rules change or when they reconnect without saved data."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Compression ratio (sent / synced)",
      "id": 32,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "powersync:compression:ratio5m{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}",
          "legendFormat": "compression ratio"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Bytes sent over the network divided by the size of the data before compression. 0.2 means clients download 20% of the original size (80% saved).\n\n**Healthy:** Lower is better: less bandwidth for mobile users and lower network cost. Values well below 1 mean compression works.\n\n**If not:** A value near 1 means the data is not compressed. Usually a proxy or load balancer between the clients and PowerSync removes the compression headers."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Bytes per connection",
      "id": 33,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "powersync:bytes_per_conn:5m{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}",
          "legendFormat": "bytes/conn"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Bytes sent per second for each connected client, before compression.\n\n**Healthy:** Stable over time for your app.\n\n**If not:** Spikes mean some clients download a lot of data, for example a first sync of large buckets or a sync rules change that makes clients download everything again."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Ops per row (fan-out)",
      "id": 34,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 31
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "powersync:ops_per_row:5m{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}",
          "legendFormat": "ops/row"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** How many operations clients download for each row that changes in the source database. Example: a row that only one user syncs gives about 1. A row in a table that all 1,000 users sync gives about 1,000.\n\n**Healthy:** Stable over time. High values are normal for data that all users share, but every change to that data is then downloaded by every user.\n\n**If not:** A value that grows, or is much higher than you expect, can mean the sync rules send data to more users than need it. First syncs and reconnects also raise this value, because clients download operations without any row changing."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sync connection errors & rejections (by code)",
      "id": 35,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome, close_reason, error_code) (increase(powersync_sync_connections_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\", outcome=~\"error|rejected\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}} \u00b7 {{close_reason}} \u00b7 {{error_code}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Sync connections that ended with an error or were rejected, per 5 minutes, by error code. Look up each code in the [error codes](https://docs.powersync.com/debugging/error-codes). Needs PowerSync Service 1.28.0 or later.\n\n**Healthy:** No data. The lines only start after the first error.\n\n**If not:** **rejected** usually means an API task reached its connection limit, so check that autoscaling adds tasks. For **error**, look up the code in the error codes page."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sync connection closes (by outcome \u00b7 reason)",
      "id": 36,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 39
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome, close_reason) (rate(powersync_sync_connections_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[5m])) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}} \u00b7 {{close_reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Sync connections that closed per minute, by result (ok, error, rejected) and reason. Needs PowerSync Service 1.28.0 or later.\n\n**Healthy:** Mostly ok / client_closed: clients go offline or close the app.\n\n**If not:** A spike in service_closed or process_shutdown usually matches a deploy or a task restart. Use Sync connection errors & rejections for the error details."
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Storage & capacity",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 47
      },
      "id": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Storage size (stacked)",
      "id": 40,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 48
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 40,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(powersync_replication_storage_size_bytes{cluster=~\"$cluster\"})",
          "legendFormat": "replication"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(powersync_operation_storage_size_bytes{cluster=~\"$cluster\"})",
          "legendFormat": "operations"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "sum(powersync_parameter_storage_size_bytes{cluster=~\"$cluster\"})",
          "legendFormat": "parameters"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Disk space PowerSync uses in its bucket storage database, in three parts, stacked (the top line is the total). **Replication**: PowerSync's copy of the source rows that it syncs. **Operations**: the changes that clients download, including old changes until compaction removes them. Usually the largest part. **Parameters**: lookup data that the sync rules use to decide which data each user gets. Usually small.\n\n**Healthy:** Grows slowly with your data.\n\n**If not:** Operations growing much faster than your source data means compaction does not keep up. See [Compacting buckets](https://docs.powersync.com/maintenance-ops/compacting-buckets). Parameters growing fast: see Parameter-storage bloat ratio."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Parameter-storage bloat ratio",
      "id": 41,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROM}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 48
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "powersync:param_bloat:ratio{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}",
          "legendFormat": "param / data"
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Parameter storage size divided by the rest of the bucket storage. Parameter storage is the lookup data the sync rules use to decide which data each user gets.\n\n**Healthy:** Low and stable, well below 0.5. An alert fires above 0.5.\n\n**If not:** A high or growing value makes each client connection slower to set up, and can cause storage query timeouts. Check sync rules whose parameter queries return many rows per user."
    },
    {
