          "namespace": "AWS/ECS",
          "metricName": "CPUUtilization",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "ClusterName": "$ecs_cluster",
            "ServiceName": "$api_service"
          },
          "label": "api",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "region": "default",
          "namespace": "AWS/ECS",
          "metricName": "CPUUtilization",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "ClusterName": "$ecs_cluster",
            "ServiceName": "$repl_service"
          },
          "label": "replication",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0
        }
      ],
      "description": "**What it shows:** Average CPU use of the API and replication tasks, in percent.\n\n**Healthy:** Below about 70% most of the time. The API autoscaler adds tasks when CPU stays high.\n\n**If not:** The replicator near 100% for a long time can cause Replication lag. API near 100% with the maximum number of tasks running means you need more or bigger tasks."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "ECS memory utilization",
      "id": 51,
      "datasource": {
